    "body": "## Summary\n\n`PostMeltQuoteResponse.from_melt_quote` is decorated with `@classmethod` but has two bugs:\n\n1. The first parameter is named `self` instead of `cls`, which is misleading and inconsistent with Python classmethod conventions.\n2. The method hardcodes `PostMeltQuoteResponse.model_validate(to_dict)` instead of using `cls.model_validate(to_dict)`, breaking correct behavior for any subclass that calls this method, it would silently return a `PostMeltQuoteResponse` instance instead of an instance of the subclass.\n\nThis is inconsistent with `PostMintQuoteResponse.from_mint_quote` in `mint_quote.py`, which correctly uses `cls`.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nCalling `SubclassOfPostMeltQuoteResponse.from_melt_quote(quote)` should return an instance of the subclass, not of `PostMeltQuoteResponse`.\n\n## Affected file\n\n`cashu/core/models/melt_quote.py`\n\n## Screenshot of report\n\n<img width=\"902\" height=\"405\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c19501d3-443f-4d9b-9467-e2bf7c5add0f\" />",
